Examine the prevailing interest rate environment and its potential impact on corporate earnings and economic growth. 
Compare current interest rates to historical averages and assess the potential effects of expected future rate changes. 
If interest rates are favorable or expected to become more favorable, lean towards a bullish sentiment and a corresponding 
conviction level reflecting the strength of the favorable conditions. 
Conversely, unfavorable interest rates or expectations of unfavorable changes should lead to a bearish sentiment with appropriate conviction.